WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:00.709 align:start position:0%
 
[Applause]  eight days after breaking the world  record carsten farhom won again in the  400 meter hurdles  this time setting a new meeting record  in monaco the norwegian all set for a  tokyo showdown with america's ride  benjamin  who is also unbeaten this year no shock  there but there was an upset in the  men's 100 meters  gold medal favorite trayvon brommell was  beaten for the first time this season  upstaged by fellow american ronnie baker  jamaican legend shelly and fraser price  went in the women's 200 meters  but could only manage third with  bahamian shaunae miller weibo  powering through to take the win by the  smallest of margins  the men's 800 featured most of the  olympic favorites  and it resulted in four of the five  fastest times in the world this year  botswana's nigel amos coming out on top  in this one  and in the women's race the podium  finishers all ran personal bests  with britain's laura muir taking her  first diamond league win at this  distance  since 2018. over the 1500  the night belonged to kenya world  champion timothy chariot took the win in  a very quick men's race  which produced the six fastest times of  the year  and it was faith kip yaegon who took the  women's race  also in a world-leading time and a new  kenyan record  in the field events the czech republic's  two-time olympic champion barbara  spotakova won the women's javelin  an american katie najat came out on top  in the women's pole vault  clearing a height of 4.9 metres  the athletes were cheered on by 8 000  spectators in monaco  but things will be a lot quieter in two  weeks time at the olympics  with fans banned from all tokyo venues  david stokes  al jazeera

